<h3>About Sony Partner Network Authentication</h3>
<p>The PlayStation Partner Portal uses <b>SONY ID SSO</b> (Sony's corporate single sign-on):</p>
<ol>
<li>Click the verification button above</li>
<li>Sign in with your Sony Partner Network credentials</li>
<li>Complete the bank verification form</li>
<li>Upload proof of bank account ownership</li>
</ol>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E3F2FD;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>What documents are required for bank verification?</b> For a corporate bank account, we require: (1) a bank statement in your company name showing the account number, (2) your company registration certificate, and (3) a letter from your finance department authorizing the account for receiving payments from SIE. If your bank is outside Japan (as yours is, in China), you'll also need to provide the SWIFT code and proof that your bank can receive USD wires. The offline_access permission is needed because the verification form has multiple sections and may take 20-30 minutes if you need to gather documents during the process.
</p>

